---
interface Props {
  stages: { name: string }[];
}

const { stages } = Astro.props;
---

<section id="interactive-demo" class="landing-section interactive-demo-section" aria-labelledby="interactive-demo-heading">
  <div class="landing-container interactive-demo">
    <header class="section-heading section-heading--split">
      <div>
        <h2 id="interactive-demo-heading">Follow a claim to the source worth checking.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>
        Trace one example from a research claim through its citation to a candidate passage, then
        see how the same trail appears in Paper Review.
      </p>
    </header>

    <aside class="demo-data-note" aria-label="Synthetic demo data notice">
      <strong>Synthetic example</strong>
      <p>All names, claims, and papers below are fictional. This static demo does not upload a document or contact a provider.</p>
    </aside>

    <div class="demo-story" data-demo-story>
      <ol class="demo-story__steps" aria-label="Five-stage Analysis Run pipeline walkthrough" hidden>
        {stages.map((stage, index) => (
          <li><button type="button" data-demo-step={index} aria-pressed={index === 0 ? "true" : "false"}>{stage.name}</button></li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <output class="demo-story__status" data-demo-step-status role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true" hidden>Step 1 of {stages.length} · {stages[0]?.name ?? "Read the PDF"}</output>

      <div class="demo-story__details">
        <article class="demo-story__panel" data-demo-story-panel="0">
          <p class="demo-story__kind">Stage 01 · {stages[0]?.name} · synthetic source document</p>
          <h3>A weekly planning routine helped first-year students complete more reading assignments.</h3>
          <p>This fictional claim is traced from a text-based source PDF; the demo does not run the claim-analysis LLM.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="demo-story__panel" data-demo-story-panel="1">
          <p class="demo-story__kind">Stage 02 · {stages[1]?.name} · synthetic citation context</p>
          <h3>A weekly planning routine helped first-year students complete more reading assignments <mark>(Rivera &amp; Holm, 2024)</mark>.</h3>
          <p>The citation marker points to a fictional bibliography entry; the demo does not query Crossref.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="demo-story__panel" data-demo-story-panel="2">
          <p class="demo-story__kind">Stage 03 · {stages[2]?.name} · synthetic cited paper</p>
          <h3>Planning routines and undergraduate reading completion</h3>
          <p>A. Rivera and M. Holm · 2024 · fictional study</p>
          <p>This fictional source stands in for eligible cited-paper text; the demo does not retrieve a paper.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="demo-story__panel" data-demo-story-panel="3">
          <p class="demo-story__kind">Stage 04 · {stages[3]?.name} · synthetic candidate passage</p>
          <blockquote>“First-year students assigned to weekly planning completed a higher share of reading assignments than first-year students who received the usual course guidance.”</blockquote>
          <p>Results · page 6. Retrieval surfaces this candidate for inspection; it does not decide whether the claim is supported.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="demo-story__panel" data-demo-story-panel="4">
          <p class="demo-story__kind">Stage 05 · {stages[4]?.name} · fictional assessment</p>
          <h3>Illustrative judgement: Direct support</h3>
          <p>The real System One LLM returns a typed Evidence Judgement. This sample is uncalibrated, not a verdict, and no model runs in this demo; researchers decide.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>

    <header class="demo-review-intro">
      <div>
        <h3>Paper Review</h3>
        <p>Inspect a source document alongside citations, bibliography details, and illustrative AI results.</p>
      </div>
      <span class="demo-review-intro__badge">Synthetic data</span>
    </header>

    <div class="demo-review-shell" data-demo-review>
      <div class="demo-review-layout">
        <section class="demo-pdf" aria-labelledby="demo-pdf-heading">
          <header class="demo-pdf__document-header">
            <div>
              <h4 id="demo-pdf-heading">Original source document</h4>
              <p>weekly-planning-study.pdf</p>
            </div>
          </header>
          <div class="demo-pdf__toolbar"><span>Excerpts from pages 3 and 8 of an 8-page paper</span></div>
          <div class="demo-pdf__pages" data-demo-pdf-pages role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Fictional PDF excerpts, pages 3 and 8">
            <article class="demo-pdf__page" aria-label="Fictional source document page 3">
              <p class="demo-pdf__notice">Synthetic source document</p>
              <h5>Digital reading and weekly planning</h5>
              <p class="demo-pdf__byline">A fictional research draft · Introduction</p>
              <p>Reading routines can help students plan their study time. Researchers have explored how small changes to weekly schedules affect course participation and assignment completion.</p>
              <p><span data-demo-pdf-text="claim">A weekly planning routine helped first-year students complete more reading assignments</span> <span data-demo-pdf-text="citation">(Rivera &amp; Holm, 2024)</span>. These findings suggest that regular planning may support students as they organize course work.</p>
              <p>Further research could examine how these routines work across different courses and student groups.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="demo-pdf__page demo-pdf__page--references" aria-label="Fictional source document page 8, bibliography">
              <p class="demo-pdf__notice">Page 8 · synthetic reference list</p>
              <h5>References</h5>
              <p class="demo-pdf__byline">Fictional bibliography entry</p>
              <p class="demo-pdf__reference-entry" data-demo-pdf-text="bibliography">Rivera, A., &amp; Holm, M. (2024). Planning routines and undergraduate reading completion. <em>Synthetic Journal of Learning Studies, 12</em>(2), 45–61.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <aside class="demo-review-details" aria-label="Paper Review details">
          <div class="demo-review-details__switcher" role="group" aria-label="Review detail type" data-demo-review-controls hidden>
            <button type="button" data-demo-review-view="results" aria-pressed="true">AI results</button>
            <button type="button" data-demo-review-view="citations" aria-pressed="false">Citations &amp; bibliography</button>
          </div>

          <section class="demo-review-details__panel" data-demo-review-panel="results" aria-labelledby="demo-results-heading">
            <div class="demo-review-details__claim-card">
              <div class="demo-review-details__claim-card-header">
                <h4 class="demo-review-details__label" id="demo-results-heading">Atomic Claim</h4>
                <div class="demo-review-details__actions" data-demo-pdf-controls hidden>
                  <button type="button" data-demo-pdf-highlight="claim" aria-pressed="false">Show claim in PDF</button>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p class="demo-review-details__claim">A weekly planning routine helped first-year students complete more reading assignments.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="demo-review-details__outcome">
              <span>Illustrative Claim–Paper result</span>
              <strong>Supported</strong>
            </div>
            <p class="demo-review-details__caveat">Example status only. Candidate passages are for inspection; the report is a human triage aid, not a truth certification.</p>
            <div class="demo-review-details__evidence-heading">
              <h5>Evidence passage</h5>
              <span class="demo-review-details__judgement">Direct support</span>
            </div>
            <blockquote>“First-year students assigned to weekly planning completed a higher share of reading assignments than first-year students who received the usual course guidance.”</blockquote>
            <p class="demo-review-details__provenance">Fictional cited paper · Results, page 6</p>
          </section>

          <section class="demo-review-details__panel" data-demo-review-panel="citations" aria-labelledby="demo-citations-heading">
            <h4 id="demo-citations-heading">Citation context</h4>
            <blockquote>A weekly planning routine helped first-year students complete more reading assignments <span>(Rivera &amp; Holm, 2024)</span>.</blockquote>
            <h5>Bibliography entry</h5>
            <p>Rivera, A., &amp; Holm, M. (2024). Planning routines and undergraduate reading completion. <em>Synthetic Journal of Learning Studies, 12</em>(2), 45–61.</p>
            <p class="demo-review-details__caveat">This citation and bibliography entry are invented for the demo.</p>
            <div class="demo-review-details__actions" data-demo-pdf-controls hidden>
              <button type="button" data-demo-pdf-highlight="citation" aria-pressed="false">Show citation in PDF</button>
              <button type="button" data-demo-pdf-highlight="bibliography" aria-pressed="false">Show bibliography in PDF</button>
            </div>
          </section>
          <output class="demo-review-details__status" data-demo-pdf-status role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></output>
        </aside>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="demo-mobile-note">The full Paper Review view is designed for larger screens in the workspace, so this preview is hidden here. The walkthrough above remains available.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const demo = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-story]");

  if (demo) {
    const stepButtons = Array.from(demo.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-demo-step]"));
    const storyPanels = Array.from(demo.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-story-panel]"));
    const stepStatus = demo.querySelector<HTMLOutputElement>("[data-demo-step-status]");

    if (stepButtons.length === storyPanels.length && stepStatus) {
      stepButtons.forEach((button, index) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          stepButtons.forEach((stepButton, stepIndex) => {
            stepButton.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(stepIndex === index));
          });
          storyPanels.forEach((panel, panelIndex) => {
            panel.hidden = panelIndex !== index;
          });
          stepStatus.textContent = `Step ${index + 1} of ${stepButtons.length} · ${stepButtons[index]?.textContent?.trim() ?? ""}`;
        });
      });

      storyPanels.forEach((panel, index) => {
        panel.hidden = index !== 0;
      });
      demo.querySelector<HTMLElement>(".demo-story__steps")?.removeAttribute("hidden");
      stepStatus.removeAttribute("hidden");
    }
  }

  const review = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-review]");

  if (review) {
    const reviewButtons = Array.from(review.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-demo-review-view]"));
    const reviewPanels = Array.from(review.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-review-panel]"));
    const pdfButtons = Array.from(review.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>("[data-demo-pdf-highlight]"));
    const pdfText = Array.from(review.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-pdf-text]"));
    const pdfPages = review.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-pdf-pages]");
    const pdfStatus = review.querySelector<HTMLOutputElement>("[data-demo-pdf-status]");

    if (reviewButtons.length === reviewPanels.length) {
      reviewButtons.forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const selectedView = button.dataset.demoReviewView;
          reviewButtons.forEach((viewButton) => {
            viewButton.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(viewButton === button));
          });
          reviewPanels.forEach((panel) => {
            panel.hidden = panel.dataset.demoReviewPanel !== selectedView;
          });
        });
      });
      reviewPanels.forEach((panel) => {
        panel.hidden = panel.dataset.demoReviewPanel !== "results";
      });
      review.querySelector<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-review-controls]")?.removeAttribute("hidden");
    }

    if (pdfButtons.length > 0 && pdfText.length > 0 && pdfPages && pdfStatus) {
      const scrollPdfToText = (target: HTMLElement) => {
        const pagesRect = pdfPages.getBoundingClientRect();
        const targetRect = target.getBoundingClientRect();
        const currentScrollTop = pdfPages.scrollTop;
        const targetTop = currentScrollTop + targetRect.top - pagesRect.top - pdfPages.clientTop;
        const targetBottom = targetTop + targetRect.height;
        const visibleBottom = currentScrollTop + pdfPages.clientHeight;

        if (targetTop >= currentScrollTop && targetBottom <= visibleBottom) return;

        const centeredScrollTop = targetTop - (pdfPages.clientHeight - targetRect.height) / 2;
        const maxScrollTop = Math.max(0, pdfPages.scrollHeight - pdfPages.clientHeight);
        const scrollTop = Math.max(0, Math.min(centeredScrollTop, maxScrollTop));
        const behavior = window.matchMedia("(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)").matches ? "auto" : "smooth";

        pdfPages.scrollTo({ top: scrollTop, behavior });
      };

      pdfButtons.forEach((button) => {
        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const selectedText = button.dataset.demoPdfHighlight;
          if (!selectedText) return;

          pdfButtons.forEach((pdfButton) => {
            pdfButton.setAttribute("aria-pressed", String(pdfButton === button));
          });
          pdfText.forEach((text) => {
            text.classList.toggle("is-highlighted", text.dataset.demoPdfText === selectedText);
          });
          const highlightedText = pdfText.find((text) => text.dataset.demoPdfText === selectedText);
          if (highlightedText) scrollPdfToText(highlightedText);
          const selectedLabel = selectedText === "claim"
            ? "Claim"
            : selectedText === "citation"
              ? "Citation"
              : "Bibliography entry";
          const pageNumber = selectedText === "bibliography" ? 8 : 3;
          pdfStatus.textContent = `${selectedLabel} highlighted in the synthetic source PDF, page ${pageNumber}.`;
        });
      });
      review.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>("[data-demo-pdf-controls]").forEach((controls) => {
        controls.removeAttribute("hidden");
      });
    }
  }
</script>

<style>
  .landing-section.interactive-demo-section {
    min-height: 0;
    background: var(--ptr-paper-bright);
  }

  .landing-section.interactive-demo-section > .landing-container.interactive-demo {
    justify-content: flex-start;
    gap: clamp(28px, 5svh, 52px);
  }

  .demo-data-note {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: max-content minmax(0, 1fr);
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 12px 20px;
    padding-block: 14px;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--ptr-border);
  }

  .demo-data-note strong {
    color: var(--ptr-teal-deep);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .demo-data-note p,
  .demo-review-intro p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ptr-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .demo-story {
    width: min(100%, 960px);
    align-self: center;
  }

  .demo-story__steps {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .demo-story__steps[hidden],
  .demo-story__status[hidden],
  .demo-review-details__switcher[hidden],
  .demo-review-details__actions[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .demo-story__steps li {
    position: relative;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .demo-story__steps li:not(:last-child)::after {
    position: absolute;
    z-index: 0;
    top: 50%;
    right: 0;
    left: 0;
    border-top: 1px dashed var(--ptr-border);
    content: "";
    transform: translateY(-50%);
  }

  .demo-story__steps button {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    width: 100%;
    min-height: 48px;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 8px;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    background: var(--ptr-paper-bright);
    color: var(--ptr-muted);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 650;
    cursor: pointer;
  }

  .demo-story__steps button[aria-pressed="true"] {
    border-color: var(--ptr-ink);
    background: var(--ptr-ink);
    color: var(--ptr-paper-bright);
  }

  .demo-story__steps button:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--ptr-focus);
    outline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .demo-review-details__switcher button:focus-visible,
  .demo-review-details__actions button:focus-visible {
    outline: none;
    border-color: var(--ptr-focus);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px color-mix(in srgb, var(--ptr-focus) 50%, transparent);
  }

  .demo-story__status {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 18px;
    color: var(--ptr-muted);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .demo-story__details {
    min-height: 208px;
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding: clamp(20px, 4vw, 36px);
    border: 1px solid var(--ptr-border);
    background: var(--ptr-paper);
  }

  .demo-story__panel[hidden],
  .demo-review-details__panel[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }

  .demo-story__kind,
  .demo-review-details__label {
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--ptr-teal-deep);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .demo-story__panel h3 {
    max-width: 34ch;
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(23px, 3.2vw, 34px);
    line-height: 1.14;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .demo-story__panel > p:last-child {
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 12px 0 0;
    color: var(--ptr-muted);
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .demo-story__panel blockquote,
  .demo-review-details__panel blockquote {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .demo-story__panel mark {
    background: var(--ptr-paper-gold);
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
  }

  .demo-review-intro {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 20px;
  }

  .demo-review-intro > div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4px;
  }

  .demo-review-intro h3 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-body);
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .demo-review-intro p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ptr-muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }

  .demo-review-intro__badge {
    display: inline-flex;
    height: 20px;
    flex: none;
    align-items: center;
    align-self: center;
    padding: 2px 8px;
    border: 1px solid var(--ptr-border);
    border-radius: 9999px;
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: normal;
    text-transform: none;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .demo-review-shell {
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--ptr-border);
    border-radius: calc(var(--ptr-radius-control) * 1.4);
    background: var(--ptr-paper-bright);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 1px color-mix(in srgb, var(--ptr-ink) 10%, transparent), 0 1px 2px color-mix(in srgb, var(--ptr-ink) 8%, transparent);
  }

  .demo-review-layout {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(19rem, 0.9fr);
    gap: 16px;
    min-height: 560px;
    padding: 12px 16px;
  }

  .demo-pdf {
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    flex-direction: column;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--ptr-border);
    border-radius: calc(var(--ptr-radius-control) * 0.8);
    background: var(--ptr-paper);
    box-shadow: 0 1px 2px color-mix(in srgb, var(--ptr-ink) 8%, transparent);
  }

  .demo-pdf__document-header {
    display: flex;
    min-width: 0;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 10px 12px;
    background: var(--ptr-paper-bright);
  }

  .demo-pdf__document-header h4 {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font-size: 14px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .demo-pdf__document-header p {
    margin: 2px 0 0;
    color: var(--ptr-muted);
    font-size: 12px;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  .demo-pdf__toolbar {
    display: flex;
    min-height: 32px;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    background: var(--ptr-ink);
    color: var(--ptr-paper-bright);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .demo-pdf__toolbar span {
    flex: none;
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
  }

  .demo-pdf__pages {
    display: grid;
    justify-items: center;
    align-content: start;
    gap: 16px;
    max-height: 520px;
    min-height: 0;
    overflow-x: hidden;
    overflow-y: auto;
    padding: 16px 8px;
    overscroll-behavior: contain;
    scroll-behavior: smooth;
    scrollbar-color: var(--ptr-border) var(--ptr-paper-soft);
    scrollbar-width: thin;
  }

  .demo-pdf__pages:focus-visible {
    outline: 3px solid var(--ptr-focus);
    outline-offset: -3px;
  }

  .demo-pdf__pages .demo-pdf__page {
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  .demo-pdf__page {
    width: min(100% - 32px, 36rem);
    min-height: 480px;
    align-self: center;
    margin: 16px auto;
    padding: clamp(22px, 4vw, 48px);
    background: var(--ptr-paper-bright);
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-display);
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px color-mix(in srgb, var(--ptr-ink) 10%, transparent);
  }

  .demo-pdf__page--references {
    min-height: 260px;
  }

  .demo-pdf__reference-entry {
    padding-left: 1.5em;
    text-indent: -1.5em;
  }

  .demo-pdf__notice {
    margin: 0 0 25px;
    color: var(--ptr-teal-deep);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-mono);
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .demo-pdf__page h5 {
    margin: 0;
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-display);
    font-size: clamp(20px, 2.3vw, 27px);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .demo-pdf__byline {
    padding-bottom: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--ptr-border);
    color: var(--ptr-muted);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-body);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  .demo-pdf__page > p:not(.demo-pdf__notice, .demo-pdf__byline) {
    margin: 18px 0 0;
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font-family: var(--ptr-font-body);
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .demo-pdf__page [data-demo-pdf-text] {
    background: transparent;
    transition: background-color 160ms ease;
  }

  .demo-pdf__page [data-demo-pdf-text].is-highlighted {
    background: var(--ptr-paper-gold);
    outline: 2px solid var(--ptr-gold-ink);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .demo-review-details {
    min-width: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }

  .demo-review-details__switcher {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: 4px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
    padding: 4px;
    border: 1px solid var(--ptr-border);
    border-radius: calc(var(--ptr-radius-control) * 1.4);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ptr-paper-muted) 60%, transparent);
  }

  .demo-review-details__switcher button {
    min-width: 0;
    min-height: 36px;
    padding: 8px;
    border: 1px solid transparent;
    border-radius: calc(var(--ptr-radius-control) * 0.8);
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--ptr-ink);
    font: inherit;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.25;
    white-space: normal;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background-color 140ms ease, color 140ms ease;
  }

  .demo-review-details__switcher button:hover {
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--ptr-ink) 6%, var(--ptr-paper-muted));
  }

  .demo-review-details__switcher button[aria-pressed="true"] {
    background: var(--ptr-red);
